Build the apk tars in ustar format. tar defaults to the GNU format, which stores paths
over 100 chars in a GNU long-name (L) entry whose size counts the trailing NUL. apk-tools
>= 3.0.9 (Alpine 3.24.4) takes that NUL as part of the file name and rejects the package
with "file format is invalid or inconsistent". ustar splits long paths into the prefix
field instead (up to 255 chars; tar errors out above that).
Applied on top of fpm_apk_tar_headers.patch.

--- a/lib/fpm/package/apk.rb
+++ b/lib/fpm/package/apk.rb
@@ -433,6 +433,9 @@
       args =
       [
         tar_cmd,
+        # ustar: long paths go in the prefix field. apk-tools 3.0.9 (Alpine 3.24.4)
+        # rejects the GNU long-name (L) entries tar writes by default for paths over 100 chars.
+        "--format=ustar",
         "-f",
         target_path,
         "-c"
